From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:56:34 -0500
Subject: feat: a tab playing in the background shows a card in the sidebar
 (S-95)

A tab of the window that plays sound while it is not on screen shows a
card at the sidebar's foot, above Archived: its favicon and title, play
or pause, and stop (docs/features/player.md Mp3, Mp7). The card's body
shows the tab in its Space. In the rail the card is the favicon above
History, and a click pauses or plays (Mp8). Option-Shift-Cmd-M
(Ctrl+Alt+Shift+M) shows the tab, and the command bar lists Go to,
Pause or Play, and Stop while a card shows (Mp9, commandbar K45). On by
default, with a setting and a command bar switch (Mp10, settings T62).
Each tab's media session is watched through its MediaSessionObserver;
the rules that pick the card's tab are a pure function with unit tests.
VideoPopOut's on-screen test is shared.

Why: Arc's media controls at the foot of the sidebar, the most asked-for
part of its mini player (GitHub discussion 104). The owner chose the
card from rendered options on 2026-11-13.
Removable when: never; Stedding's own sidebar.
